From: PS5 Linux Kernel Team <kernel@ps5-linux.local>
Subject: [PATCH 1/12] mt7921e: disable runtime PM and deep sleep on PS5 Salina southbridge

Sony Salina southbridge does not implement PCIe ASPM L1.1/L1.2 substate
handshaking. When MT7921 enters runtime PM or deep sleep, the Salina
interconnect drops power and clocks to the endpoint, returning 0xffffffff
on subsequent MMIO accesses. This cascades into xHCI host controller failure
and triggers a PMIC hard power shutdown approximately 20 seconds after boot.

Gate dev->pm.enable, dev->pm.ds_enable, and their user counterparts on
!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86_PS5) to keep the MT7921 chip fully in D0 state.

Signed-off-by: PS5 Linux Kernel Team <kernel@ps5-linux.local>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/init.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/init.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/init.c
index a41bc8f..d79a25b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/init.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/init.c
@@ -209,12 +209,24 @@ int mt7921_register_device(struct mt792x_dev *dev)
 	dev->pm.stats.last_wake_event = jiffies;
 	dev->pm.stats.last_doze_event = jiffies;
 
 	if (!mt76_is_usb(&dev->mt76) &&
 	    !is_mt7902(&dev->mt76)) {
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86_PS5)
+		/*
+		 * Sony Salina Southbridge drops PCIe interconnect clock/power when MT7921
+		 * enters runtime PM or deep sleep, causing bus read 0xffffffff and hard
+		 * console power shutdown ~20s after boot. Keep MT7921 fully in D0.
+		 */
+		dev->pm.enable_user = false;
+		dev->pm.enable = false;
+		dev->pm.ds_enable_user = false;
+		dev->pm.ds_enable = false;
+#else
 		dev->pm.enable_user = true;
 		dev->pm.enable = true;
 		dev->pm.ds_enable_user = true;
 		dev->pm.ds_enable = true;
+#endif
 	}
 
 	if (!mt76_is_mmio(&dev->mt76))
-- 
